Conclusion
When tackling train scheduling or simulation problems, careful consideration of the following can lead to robust and efficient solutions:

Thoroughly understanding the problem statement and constraints.
Properly sorting and handling simultaneous events.
Using the right data structures for efficient simulation.
Testing against edge cases to ensure accuracy.
By keeping these common pitfalls in mind, you can confidently approach train problems and avoid typical errors that lead to incorrect or inefficient implementations.


